WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.551
Zann knew he should try to get away before the troll grabbed him.

2
00:00:03.552 --> 00:00:06.190
But the collision had knocked the breath out of him.

3
00:00:06.191 --> 00:00:10.942
All he could do was stare at the creature's broad chest, inches from his face.

4
00:00:10.943 --> 00:00:13.104
A glint of silver caught his eye.

5
00:00:13.105 --> 00:00:15.977
A small talisman hung around the troll's neck.

6
00:00:15.978 --> 00:00:21.596
It was slim and delicate, so tiny that Zann never would have spotted it from a distance.

7
00:00:21.597 --> 00:00:24.619
Zing let out a whistle and flew at the troll.

8
00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:29.406
Ignoring Zing's attack, the troll shoved Zann aside and hurried down the corridor.

9
00:00:29.407 --> 00:00:32.224
The troll hardly seemed to have noticed the kids at all.

10
00:00:32.225 --> 00:00:39.870
A puff of magic energy was floating above its ugly head, showing a chaotic image of running Reds and a pile of turnips.

11
00:00:39.871 --> 00:00:43.075
"Wow, that was close!" Gliss exclaimed.

12
00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:47.816
"Yeah. Why did that troll let me go?" Zann wondered.

13
00:00:47.817 --> 00:00:51.146
"It didn't even seem to see you," said Perda.

14
00:00:51.147 --> 00:00:53.467
Darb was staring after the creature.

15
00:00:53.468 --> 00:00:57.574
"Trolls have trouble thinking about more than one thing at a time," he said.

16
00:00:57.575 --> 00:01:02.169
"It looked like that one was running to tell Morb about the escaped prisoners at the zoo.

17
00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:05.067
It probably barely noticed we were in the way."

18
00:01:05.068 --> 00:01:10.857
"Lucky for us," Zann said. "Now let's get out of here!"

19
00:01:10.858 --> 00:01:14.175
Wyssa picked up the battered old brass pot.

20
00:01:14.176 --> 00:01:19.110
In Magica there was no need for the tonics and potions she'd learned to mix as a child.

21
00:01:19.111 --> 00:01:25.895
But she often needed such things in her travels, especially to those dangerous places that didn't have any natural magic.

22
00:01:25.896 --> 00:01:31.651
After placing the pot carefully into a large cloth bag, Wyssa straightened up with a groan.

23
00:01:31.652 --> 00:01:34.989
Years of traveling had been hard on her body.

24
00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:40.168
Her gaze fell on a worn blink image of a happy family, and she grimaced.

25
00:01:40.169 --> 00:01:43.197
Some of her travels had been hard on her soul too.

26
00:01:43.198 --> 00:01:49.673
Picking up the picture, she forced herself to stare at the smiling faces—especially that of the Red boy.

27
00:01:49.674 --> 00:01:52.833
Keeping the image around reminded her to be careful.

28
00:01:52.834 --> 00:01:57.051
That was why she was leaving the home she'd made for herself in Wormwood.

29
00:01:57.052 --> 00:01:59.695
And this time she wasn't coming back.

30
00:01:59.696 --> 00:02:05.236
She had one last errand to run, one last item she'd promised Morb.

31
00:02:05.237 --> 00:02:08.821
Then she was going somewhere he could never find her.

32
00:02:08.822 --> 00:02:12.936
Whatever happened next in Magica, she wouldn't be responsible.

33
00:02:12.937 --> 00:02:17.882
As she tucked the picture into her bag, Wyssa heard a shuffling step outside her hut.

34
00:02:17.883 --> 00:02:24.674
Looking out, she saw Hap staring curiously at the pile of objects she'd put outside the entrance.

35
00:02:24.675 --> 00:02:29.540
"Going somewhere, Wyssa?" the Void asked in his hoarse, high-pitched voice.

36
00:02:29.541 --> 00:02:33.657
"We're all going somewhere, my friend," she responded.

37
00:02:33.658 --> 00:02:39.666
"As for me, it's time for choice to put an end to what chance has started."

38
00:02:39.667 --> 00:02:44.141
Hap blinked at her. "Eh? What do you mean by that?"

39
00:02:44.142 --> 00:02:48.232
"Never mind." Wyssa waved an arm at the pile.

40
00:02:48.233 --> 00:02:51.876
"If there's anything you'd like in there, you're welcome to it.

41
00:02:51.877 --> 00:02:54.588
You can have my hut too, for that matter.

42
00:02:54.589 --> 00:02:59.366
You've been as good a neighbor as one could expect in a place like this."

43
00:02:59.367 --> 00:03:03.580
She cast a glance around Wormwood. She wouldn't miss it.

44
00:03:03.581 --> 00:03:10.579
Hap's eyes went wide. "My thanks to you, Wyssa," he said, shooting a greedy look at the hut.

45
00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:16.302
"It'll do my old bones good to have a roof over my head for a change."

46
00:03:16.303 --> 00:03:23.639
Wyssa went back inside just long enough to grab a few more items, which she stuffed into her bag. The rest didn't matter.

47
00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:29.701
"You're welcome," she told Hap, who was already admiring a frayed hat he'd found in the pile.

48
00:03:29.702 --> 00:03:32.642
"Good luck to you in the days ahead."

49
00:03:32.643 --> 00:03:41.114
Hap muttered another "thanks," though he didn't look up as Wyssa stepped toward the old tree without a backward glance.

50
00:03:41.115 --> 00:03:45.220
"I can't believe Morb just declared himself king like that,"

51
00:03:45.221 --> 00:03:50.303
Perda said for about the tenth time since she, Zann, and the others had escaped from the palace.

52
00:03:50.304 --> 00:03:56.478
"It's not as if anybody could stop him," Gliss reminded her. "You saw what he did."

53
00:03:56.479 --> 00:04:04.291
"Yeah," Zann agreed. "He's got tons of power, all of it stolen from the Reds he kidnapped."

54
00:04:04.292 --> 00:04:10.120
Zann clenched his fists as he walked, thinking about Boz and Teplo and all the others.

55
00:04:10.121 --> 00:04:15.561
"Not to mention those horrible little dragons and all those trolls," Darb added.

56
00:04:15.562 --> 00:04:23.002
Zann shuddered when he thought back to his close call with the troll. "Hey, that reminds me," he said.

57
00:04:23.003 --> 00:04:26.807
"The troll I ran into was wearing a talisman around its neck.

58
00:04:26.808 --> 00:04:32.624
I've been wondering if that's how Morb is feeding the extra magical energy to the trolls.

59
00:04:32.625 --> 00:04:35.799
Maybe all of them are wearing talismans."

60
00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:40.367
"That would explain why the trolls have so much power," said Perda.

61
00:04:40.368 --> 00:04:46.309
"It might also explain how Morb is able to feed magic to them remotely," said Zann.

62
00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:51.403
"They became more powerful when we were at the zoo, and Morb wasn't even there."

63
00:04:51.404 --> 00:04:54.533
"We should tell Fala about this," said Darb.

64
00:04:54.534 --> 00:04:57.881
"She might know how talismans like that work."

65
00:04:57.882 --> 00:05:01.909
They'd slowed to a walk a couple of blocks earlier to catch their breath.

66
00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:05.878
The mention of Fala's name reminded Zann that they needed to hurry.

67
00:05:05.879 --> 00:05:10.928
The sooner they told Fala what was happening, the sooner she could help them think of a plan.

68
00:05:10.929 --> 00:05:14.368
"Come on, let's run," he suggested.

69
00:05:14.369 --> 00:05:18.944
Zing let out a whistle, flying faster as the kids broke into a jog.

70
00:05:18.945 --> 00:05:22.379
Soon they were just a few blocks from the safe house.

71
00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:25.849
"I hope Fala's back by now," Gliss said.

72
00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:31.507
Zann hoped so too. He also hoped that Fala would have some ideas for stopping Morb.

73
00:05:31.508 --> 00:05:43.012
Because with the palace under Morb's control and most Reds trapped in Morb's dungeon, Zann and his friends were probably Magica's only hope.

